

I’d like to talk about a time when my best friend persuaded me to try swimming, and I’m really glad that I listened to him.

It happened during my final year of high school when I was preparing for the national entrance examination to get into my dream university. At that time, I was under a huge amount of pressure because I spent most of my time studying, which left me mentally exhausted and stressed.

Fortunately, I had a very close friend who often hung out with me on weekends. He noticed that I wasn’t in a good mental state and suggested that I try swimming to relax and improve my health. Since he was a swimming enthusiast who had won several medals in local competitions, his advice sounded quite convincing.

So one day, I decided to go with him to a community swimming pool and start learning. To be honest, I initially thought swimming would be easy, but it turned out to be much harder than I expected. On my first day, I struggled to stay afloat and control my breathing underwater. However, my friend was very patient and guided me step by step, which helped me gain confidence gradually.

After several months of practicing regularly, I became much more comfortable in the water and could swim quite confidently. More importantly, swimming helped me reduce stress and improve both my physical and mental health.

Looking back, I think that experience taught me the importance of having supportive friends who genuinely care about you. It also encouraged me to step out of my comfort zone and try new things.
